AOT code caches: block linking only through data (FEX 14c9268, on top of 0002)

With AOTCodeCacheWIP, jump thunks no longer carry their ExitFunctionLinkData
record. The record lives in the AOT data area (three slots, numbered with the
data slots of 0002) and the thunk reaches it with adrp + add
(RELOC_GUEST_RIP_LINK_RECORD):

    adrp TMP1, Record; add TMP1, TMP1, :lo12:Record
    ldr TMP2, [TMP1]; cbz TMP2, 1f; br TMP2
 1: mov lr, TMP1; ldr TMP2, [STATE, ExitFunctionLinker]; br TMP2

The loader fills each record with HostCode 0, the guest RIP and CallerOffset
DATA_ONLY_LINK_RECORD. For such records ExitFunctionLink only stores HostCode
and the delinker only clears it, so neither the call site nor the thunk is
ever patched. Thunks with a patch site (ARM64EC) keep the old form.

